msgid "Modularity SPI reference"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This document describes the build items that extension authors use to "
"integrate with the xref:modularity.adoc[Quarkus modularity] system.\n"
"Extensions can declare boot modules, add inter-module dependencies, and "
"consume the completed module model."
msgstr ""

msgid "This technology is considered {extension-status}."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In _experimental_ mode, early feedback is requested to mature the idea.\n"
"There is no guarantee of stability nor long term presence in the platform "
"until the solution matures.\n"
"Feedback is welcome on our https://groups.google.com/d/forum/quarkus-"
"dev[mailing list] or as issues in our https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/"
"issues[GitHub issue tracker]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For a full list of possible statuses, check our https://quarkus.io/faq/#what-"
"are-the-extension-statuses[FAQ entry]."
msgstr ""

msgid "<code>BootModulePathBuildItem</code>"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`BootModulePathBuildItem` is a `MultiBuildItem` produced by extensions.\n"
"It declares that a named module must be placed on the boot module path."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"An extension should produce this item when it provides a module that must be "
"in the JDK's boot module layer.\n"
"This is necessary when the module is required before the dynamic module "
"loader (`smallrye-modules`) starts, or when the module must participate in "
"the boot class loading chain."
msgstr ""

msgid "The constructor takes a single `String` parameter: the module name."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The modularity extension computes the transitive closure of all declared "
"boot modules.\n"
"If a boot module depends on other modules (via `LINKED` dependencies), those "
"modules are also included in the boot set automatically.\n"
"Automatic modules are excluded from the boot set because they cannot be "
"linked by `jlink`."
msgstr ""

msgid "<code>AddDependencyBuildItem</code>"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`AddDependencyBuildItem` is a `MultiBuildItem` produced by extensions.\n"
"It adds a dependency between two modules at build time."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"An extension should produce this item when it needs to wire a module "
"dependency that is not expressed in the Maven POM or in the module's `module-"
"info.class` descriptor.\n"
"This is common when Quarkus extensions generate code that references types "
"from another module, or when service loading relationships must be declared "
"explicitly."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The constructor takes three parameters: the source module name (`String`), "
"the target module name (`String`), and a set of dependency modifiers "
"(`Modifiers<Dependency.Modifier>`)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When multiple items declare the same source/target pair, their modifier sets "
"are merged."
msgstr ""

msgid "<code>ApplicationModuleInfoBuildItem</code>"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`ApplicationModuleInfoBuildItem` is a `SimpleBuildItem` produced by the "
"modularity extension.\n"
"It contains the completed `AppModuleModel`, which includes the module "
"descriptor for every module in the application, the set of boot modules, and "
"the set of JDK modules in use."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This item is consumed by downstream packaging extensions such as the xref:"
"jlink.adoc[jlink extension].\n"
"Extension authors generally do not need to consume this item unless they are "
"implementing a custom packaging step."
msgstr ""

msgid "Dependency modifiers"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `Dependency.Modifier` enum (from `io.smallrye.modules.desc`) defines the "
"following values.\n"
"These are used with `AddDependencyBuildItem` to control how the dependency "
"is wired."
msgstr ""

msgid "`LINKED`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The dependency is linked for class loading.\n"
"Classes from the target module are visible to the source module's class "
"loader."
msgstr ""

msgid "`READ`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The dependency is readable from the source module.\n"
"Exported packages from the target module are accessible to the source module."
""
msgstr ""

msgid "`SERVICES`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Service implementations in the target module are available to the source "
"module via `ServiceLoader`."
msgstr ""

msgid "`OPTIONAL`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The dependency is optional.\n"
"If the target module is not present at link time, the dependency is silently "
"ignored rather than causing a failure."
msgstr ""

msgid "`TRANSITIVE`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The dependency is transitive.\n"
"Any module that depends on the source module also implicitly depends on the "
"target module."
msgstr ""

msgid "`SYNTHETIC`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The dependency was added by a framework rather than declared in the original "
"module descriptor. _Note:_ because modifier sets are merged when a "
"dependency is declared in two places, this modifier would take precedence "
"over a non-synthetic dependency, which is a minor detail but possibly "
"undesirable. Thus, this modifier may change to be \"non-synthetic\" or "
"something along those lines in the final version, so that an explicit "
"dependency will never be marked as being synthetic."
msgstr ""

msgid "`MANDATED`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The dependency is mandated by specification (for example, the implicit "
"dependency on `java.base`)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Related core build items"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `quarkus-core-deployment` module provides two additional build items "
"that affect the module graph.\n"
"These are documented separately but are noted here for completeness."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`ModuleOpenBuildItem` declares that one module should open specified "
"packages to another module (equivalent to the `--add-opens` JVM flag).\n"
"`ModuleEnableNativeAccessBuildItem` declares that a module requires native "
"access (equivalent to the `--enable-native-access` JVM flag)."
msgstr ""
